A component with state of its own and a rest slot, instantiated under a
reactive `for` with bare children, on every target.

Under a `for` a component with state is built at run time, and on html, fyne
and gtk4 that means a factory or a record emitted from the declaration alone.
The children are written at the call site, so the declaration's body still
held the `children` insertion and all three panicked in irwalk on an
`*ir.SlotInst`. passInstanceSlots gives the instantiation a copy of `Card`,
`Card__slot0`, with the children spliced in at the insertion. What they read
from the caller crosses as a prop the render writes per copy (`__p0` is `it`),
and the `pick` handler as an event whose body stays in the loop, where `it` is
bound -- the vocabulary passSlotChildInstances already uses for a slot child.
That is what makes adding an item render a card with its content, and a reused
card show the item now at its position.

The second `Card` is given nothing, so it keeps the declaration, and its
insertion renders the fallback block. That panicked the same way.

android passes the children as a composable parameter and bubbletea splices
the component with a cell per copy, so neither needed the pass; both are here
because the program is theirs too.
cmd/sngl/testdata/runtime_instance_bare_children_runs.txt runs it.

deny out/none/html/index.html `"item " \+ it\b` -- inside the copy the loop variable is a prop cell; a bare `it` names a binding only the page's loop has
deny out/go/fyne/model.go `"item " \+ it\b` -- as above, for the fyne record
deny out/go/gtk4/model.go `"item " \+ it\b` -- as above, for the gtk4 record
-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
        fyne
        gtk4
    }
    kotlin {
        android
    }
    none {
        html
    }
}

component Card(children ...component) node {
    var hits = 0

    vbox {
        button(text="hit {hits}", @click { hits = hits + 1 })
        children {
            text(value="empty")
        }
    }
}

var items = ["a", "b"]
var picked = ""

window {
    vbox {
        button(text="add", @click { items.push("c") })
        text(value="picked {picked}")
        for var it = items {
            Card {
                text(value="item {it}")
                button(text="pick", @click { picked = it })
            }
        }
        for var it = items {
            Card
        }
    }
}
